<text class="st-s" x="607" y="284">the number is produced some other way,</text>
<text class="st-s" x="607" y="304">and the trace narrates it afterwards</text>
<text class="st-tag op" x="410" y="342">THE LANDING GAP IS EQUALLY CONSISTENT WITH BOTH OF THESE, WHICH IS WHY THIS PROJECT EXISTS</text>
</svg>
<div class="dcap">The mirrored design, the statistic it produces, and the two accounts that
statistic cannot tell apart</div>
</div>

<h2 class="uhead">Validity trunk — is there a behaviour here to localize?</h2>
<p class="lede">Before looking inside the model it is worth checking that the effect this project
exists to explain is present in a model small enough to instrument. It largely is not, and that
is the first finding.</p>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">Screening — does any small model show the phenotype?</span>
<span class="idx">{{w1_q3_n}} no-bet + {{w2_n_side}}/side incentive rollouts per model</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>The ambiguity:</b> the predecessor result was measured on a panel of large
API-served models. Nothing guaranteed that a model small enough to run with activation hooks on
one GPU would show the same behaviour, and a localization project needs a behaviour to localize.
Five candidates were pre-registered smallest-first, before any incentive rollout existed.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Held fixed:</b> the prompts, imported rather than copied from the frozen
upstream repository so they cannot drift; the threshold construction; the sampler at temperature
{{conv_temperature}} and top-p {{conv_top_p}}, which are upstream's own effective defaults, so the
comparison to the black-box result stays meaningful.</div>
<div class="row"><b>What separates the branches:</b> a real behavioural effect should show a
landing-gap interval that excludes zero on the extractor of record <i>and</i> agreement from a
second, independent extractor. An apparatus problem should show up as the two extractors
disagreeing.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> Of five candidates, one was gated and
inaccessible, two were ineligible because the frozen deterministic extractor could not read their
answers at all ({{w1_rq_dis}} % and {{w1_rl_dis}} % disagreement against a {{lf_disagree_threshold}} %
bar), and <b>both survivors failed the gate</b>. <code>Qwen3-8B</code> gave
{{w2_gap_q3_judge_gt}} with a lower bound of exactly {{w2_ci_lo_q3}};
<code>Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct</code> gave {{w2_gap_q25_judge_gt}}
[{{w2_ci_lo_q25}}, {{w2_ci_hi_q25}}] on the extractor of record but its second extractor's
interval also included zero.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip no">GATE FAILED</span>
<span class="claim">No small model cleared the pre-registered screen, and the project continued
only by an owner-approved scope change, not by re-scoring the gate.
<span class="why">The failure is reported as a result rather than as a detour: it is the first
evidence that the prompt-stated landing gap is weaker in this model class than the black-box
panel suggested, and everything downstream inherits that weakness.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="conn"><span class="cbar"></span><span class="clab">THE SURVIVING NUMBER, RE-MEASURED</span><span class="cbar"></span><span class="ctri"></span></div>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">The winner's curse — does the screening estimate replicate?</span>
<span class="idx">{{w3_n_side}} per side, fresh seeds</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>The ambiguity:</b> the gap that justified choosing this model,
{{w2_gap_q25_judge_gt}}, was the largest of several noisy estimates, and a gate that selects the
largest selects the one luck inflated most. Nothing in the screen itself could say whether that
had happened.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Held fixed:</b> everything. The prompt text, the templated prompt, the model,
the threshold and its rendering, the inference-engine version {{conv_vllm}}, the prompt token
count and the sampler are byte-identical between the two measurements. <b>The seed block is the
only difference.</b></div>
<div class="row"><b>What separates the branches:</b> a real effect of that size should reproduce
at three times the sample; a selection artifact should collapse toward zero and the fresh blocks
should agree with each other rather than with the screen.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> The gap collapses from
<b>{{w2_gap_q25_judge_gt}}</b> to <b>{{w3_gap_A_judge_gt}}</b>, interval
[{{w3_ci_lo_A}}, {{w3_ci_hi_A}}]. On the arm where the two disagree most, screening read
{{wc_w2_above_k}}/{{wc_w2_above_n}} against {{wc_w3_above_k}}/{{wc_w3_above_n}} —
z = {{wc_z}}, two-sided p = {{wc_p}}. The three fresh blocks of {{w2_n_side}} agree with one
another ({{wc_b0_k}}/{{wc_b0_n}}, {{wc_b1_k}}/{{wc_b1_n}}, {{wc_b2_k}}/{{wc_b2_n}}) and disagree
with the screen.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip no">REJECTED</span>
<span class="claim">The screening gap was a selection artifact and is never used as an effect size
[measured].
<span class="why">Screening's two arms were extreme in opposite directions and the gap is their
difference, so both deviations added. The gate's own recorded caveat — that the screen was
underpowered — was correct, and the pivot it justified rested on a number that did not
survive.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="conn"><span class="cbar"></span><span class="clab">SO WHAT IS THE BEHAVIOUR?</span><span class="cbar"></span><span class="ctri"></span></div>

<div class="node ref">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">Refinement · the behaviour is overt, asymmetric, and a
mixture</span></div>
<div class="row">The aggregate gap is near zero on the original surface form, but the traces are
not silent. The model mentions the bet, the threshold or the cause in
<b>{{w3_mention_k}} of {{w3_mention_n}}</b> incentive traces ({{w3_mention_pct}} %), against about
{{lf_covert_pct}} % spontaneous disclosure in the {{lf_panel_size}}B panel of the predecessor
study. <b>This model does not leak a preference; it announces one</b> [measured]; the cross-scale
reading is [suggested], because two model families and no sweep separate the two studies.</div>
<div class="row">Conditioning on whether a trace's own text gets the mapping right splits the null
aggregate into two large opposite effects: traces that understand which side is favoured show
{{w3_cond_gap_A}} and {{w3_cond_gap_B}} on the two surface forms, and traces that get it wrong
show {{w3_condnot_gap_A}} and {{w3_condnot_gap_B}}. The comprehension rate itself is what makes
the aggregate small: the arm where <i>exceeding</i> the threshold is favoured is understood
{{w3_correct_A_above}} % of the time, against {{w3_correct_B_below}}–{{w3_correct_A_below}} % for
its mirror.</div>
<div class="row"><b>What this does not license:</b> the judge reads the same text the estimate came
from, so a trace saying "I will go above τ so the good cause benefits" is scored correct
<i>and</i> lands above. A large conditional gap is therefore partly guaranteed by construction.
What survives that objection is the marginal comprehension rate, which is read from
prompt-plus-text alone.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip ok">SURVIVES</span>
<span class="claim">The operative variable is not the side the prompt favours but the side the
trace believes is favoured, and the interp target moves accordingly [measured].
<span class="why">Computing the direction within a single prompt condition — contrasting traces
that believe different things while reading identical text — also removes the confound that the
prompt states the answer, which is a stronger control than the mirrored design
gives.</span></span></div>
</div>

<h2 class="uhead">Is the believed side represented?</h2>
<p class="lede">A linear probe on the residual stream, at the positions where the model writes its
own intermediate estimates, and before it names a cause.</p>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">The value direction and its probe</span>
<span class="idx">{{n_w4_points}} positions over {{n_w4_traces}} traces</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>The manipulation:</b> every stored trace is replayed through the model with a
hook on each of the {{lf_n_layers}} decoder-layer outputs, and activations are kept only at typed
positions. The load-bearing kind is an <i>estimate point</i>: a numeric literal the model wrote in
its own reasoning, inside a window around τ, with any literal exactly equal to τ excluded. The
direction is the difference in means between traces that believe above is favoured and traces that
believe below, taken <b>within the single prompt condition</b> where both classes occur.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Held fixed:</b> a trace's points are averaged before the classes are compared,
so a verbose trace cannot set the direction on its own; and the comparison is stratified on
whether the literal is itself above or below τ, so the direction cannot be a proxy for "this
number is large". The labels were frozen before any activation was read.</div>
<div class="row"><b>What separates the branches:</b> if the belief is linearly present, a probe
should beat a permutation null built from the same traces. If the pipeline is broken instead, the
positive controls on the same points through the same fit should fail too.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> On the reskin the probe reaches balanced accuracy
<b>{{w5_B_balacc_lstar}}</b> against a null {{lf_ci_pct}}th percentile of {{w5_B_null_lstar}}
(p = {{w5_B_p_lstar}}), significant at <b>{{w5_B_nsig}} of {{w5_n_layers}}</b> layers and peaking
at {{w5_B_peak}}. On the original form it is flat at every layer — while the positive controls on
those same points reach {{w5_A_dt_peak}} and {{w5_A_bp_lstar}}. And
<b>{{lf_w5_before_B}} of {{lf_w5_total_B}}</b> of the carrying points fall <i>before</i> the trace
first names a cause.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip ok">SURVIVES</span>
<span class="claim">The believed favoured side is linearly decodable from the residual stream at
estimate positions, before it is verbalized [measured].
<span class="why">The flat form is not evidence of absence: it carries {{w5_A_minority}}
minority-class traces, so power and absence are not separable there and neither is claimed. The
one informative asymmetry is that a probe trained on that form's points predicts the other form's
traces at {{w5_transfer_peak}}, which is what a signal too weakly cross-validated to see
looks like.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="conn"><span class="cbar"></span><span class="clab">A REPRESENTATION EXISTS — IS IT CAUSAL?</span><span class="cbar"></span><span class="ctri"></span></div>

<div class="fork">
<div class="fbranch"><div class="fbt">Upstream state</div><div class="fbd">The decoded direction
is the state the estimate is computed from. Writing it back in should move the landing rate in the
direction its sign predicts, and should do so more than a random direction of the same size
does.</div></div>
<div class="fbranch"><div class="fbt">Annotation</div><div class="fbd">The direction is a readable
correlate the model writes alongside an estimate produced elsewhere. Writing it back in should
move the commentary, or nothing, but not the number in a side-specific way.</div></div>
</div>

<h2 class="uhead">The intervention</h2>
<p class="lede">One causal rung, pre-registered in full — sign, layer, dose grid, null directions,
outcome table — and committed {{lf_pr005_lead}} before the first steered token existed.</p>

