<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">Injecting the direction, {{n_w7_arms}} arms × {{conv_n_per_arm}}
generations</span><span class="idx">{{n_w7_gens}} steered generations</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>The sign was frozen first.</b> The direction is defined as
mean(believes-above) − mean(believes-below), so positive α was pre-registered to <i>raise</i> the
share of answers above τ. No result is reported with that sign flipped.</div>
<div class="row"><b>What separates the branches, decided before the data:</b> a statistic counts as
a direction-specific effect only if it exceeds <i>every one</i> of the
{{n_null_directions}} random directions. If the landing rate moves and the verbalized belief moves
with it, the belief is upstream and the trace tracks it. If landing moves and the talk does not,
the direction acts on the estimate policy. If the talk moves and landing does not, the direction
writes commentary only. If neither moves, the direction is correlational.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> The primary contrast is
<b>{{w7_dplus}}</b> — the pre-registered direction's opposite — and it beats
<b>{{w7_dplus_beats}} of {{n_w7_nulls}}</b> random directions (one-sided p = {{w7_dplus_p}}).
The verbalized-belief flip has the predicted sign, {{w7_flip}}, but its interval
[{{w7_flip_lo}}, {{w7_flip_hi}}] includes zero; the entire contrast is the negative arm moving
({{w7_flip_plus_vs_sham}} against sham for +α, {{w7_flip_minus_vs_sham}} for −α); it does not
move at all in the mirrored condition ({{w7_below_phat_ap2}} against {{w7_below_phat_am2}}); and a
random direction reached {{w7_null04_phat}} where the value direction reached
{{w7_phat_ap2}}.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip no">ROW FOUR FIRED</span>
<span class="claim">Neither landing nor verbalization moved with α beyond what a random direction
of the same size does: v_p̂ is correlational [measured null].
<span class="why">The interpretation table was frozen before a single steered token existed, and
this is the row it resolved to. The result is reported at the volume the pre-registration promised
a positive result would have received.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="conn"><span class="cbar"></span><span class="clab">BUT SOMETHING DID MOVE</span><span class="cbar"></span><span class="ctri"></span></div>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">The dose anatomy — a large effect, pointing the wrong
way</span><span class="idx">{{n_w7_dose_gens}} generations across the ladder</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>What came back:</b> the injection is not inert. At the largest dose the median
estimate falls about three orders of magnitude and the landing rate falls from {{w7_P_sham}} to
{{w7_P_ap4}}. But the profile is an <b>inverted U centred exactly on the zero-dose arm</b>: it
falls on both sides, which no side-specific account predicts. At the one dose where the random
directions were also run, the value direction lands <i>below all {{n_null_directions}} of
them</i>.</div>
<div class="row"><b>The control that decides it:</b> the no-bet arm. That prompt contains no bet,
no threshold and no favoured side, so a direction acting on the believed favoured side has nothing
to act on there. The same ±α injection still moves its median estimate by
{{w7_neutral_logdelta}} log units and its above-τ rate by {{w7_neutral_dpm_abs}}.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> Landing by dose: {{w7_P_am4}} at α = −4,
{{w7_P_am2}}, {{w7_P_am1}}, <b>{{w7_P_sham}} at zero dose</b>, {{w7_P_ap1}}, {{w7_P_ap2}},
{{w7_P_ap4}} at α = +4. Monotone in α: <b>{{sk_monotone}}</b>. The {{n_null_directions}} random
directions shift landing by {{w7_null_mean}} on average — the same kind of effect, pointing the
same way, with no believed side involved at all.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip no">REJECTED</span>
<span class="claim">The large effect is direction-independent magnitude suppression, not
belief-steering [measured].
<span class="why">The most economical description of the decoded direction is a vector with a
large component along <i>estimated numeric magnitude</i>, whose believed-side content — real
enough to decode at {{w5_B_balacc_lstar}} — is not what dominates when it is written back
in.</span></span></div>
</div>

