<h2 class="uhead">The methodological finding</h2>
<p class="lede">Three pre-registrations each froze the right statistic at a setting their own
design could not resolve, and the third is the clearest case because its floor can be computed
exactly.</p>

<div class="node neu">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">A gate set below its own noise floor</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>What was frozen:</b> the low-dose follow-up needed a way to say "this dose does
not distort the model", so it pre-registered a distortion statistic — the mean, over eight random
arms, of the absolute difference between each arm's landing rate and the control's — and declared
distortion above {{lf_dbar_line}}.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Why that is a mistake independent of the data:</b> that statistic averages
absolute differences between binomial proportions at n = {{conv_n_per_arm}}. It cannot be zero
even when nothing is happening. Its expectation under the exact null the gate exists to detect —
every arm the same coin, the injection doing nothing at all — is <b>{{sk_dbar_E}}</b>, which is
already above the line the gate was given.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> Under a design doing nothing whatsoever the gate
fires with probability <b>{{sk_dbar_P}}</b>. The two interpretation rows that would have licensed
any statement <i>about the direction</i> were therefore jointly unreachable before a single token
was generated. Observed D̄ was {{w7b_dbar}}, so the "even this dose distorts" row fired and stands
as the verdict of record — while every independent indicator says these doses do not distort:
coherence {{w7b_coh}} in all {{n_w7b_arms}} arms, {{w7b_degen}} degenerate generations in
{{n_w7b_gens}}, and engagement with the bet <i>higher</i> than at the larger doses.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip op">RECORDED, NOT REPAIRED</span>
<span class="claim">Freezing a rule before the data is necessary and is not sufficient: a
pre-registration must also freeze evidence that its chosen setting and threshold lie inside the
range the design can resolve.
<span class="why">The fix is minutes of laptop arithmetic — simulate the frozen statistic under
its own null before fixing the line. No pre-registration in this project ever did it, and each of
the three paid for it in a different currency: one froze the right statistic at the wrong layer,
one at the wrong dose, one at an unreachable threshold.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="dia">
