<h2 class="uhead">Wave 2 — the same belief, through the text channel</h2>
<p class="lede">Five packets, authorised after the activation null, that ask whether the null is
the world or the instrument. Two intervene on the wording that carries the belief; two attack the
decodability result itself; the last returns to activations with a different operation.</p>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">Move comprehension, and the landing gap moves with it — both ways</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>What was varied:</b> one clarifying sentence added to the bet note
({{lf_prompt_w3}} → {{lf_prompt_w11}} prompt tokens), and separately the two mapping sentences
replaced by a semantically identical nested negation at <i>exactly</i> {{lf_prompt_w14}} tokens,
so the second manipulation adds no length at all. Nothing else changed.</div>
<div class="row"><b>What was held fixed:</b> the prediction. The four belief-conditional cells
frozen on the original dataset were asked, in advance, what landing gap each new comprehension
rate implies.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> Comprehension {{w14_pa_w3}} →
<b>{{w11_pa}}</b> raised the gap to <b>{{w11_gap}}</b> [{{w11_gap_lo}}, {{w11_gap_hi}}] against a
prediction of {{w11_pred}} [{{w11_pred_lo}}, {{w11_pred_hi}}]; comprehension {{w14_pa_w3}} →
<b>{{w14_pa}}</b> collapsed it to <b>{{w14_gap}}</b> [{{w14_gap_lo}}, {{w14_gap_hi}}] against
{{w14_pred}} [{{w14_pred_lo}}, {{w14_pred_hi}}]. Both land inside prediction, at distinguishing
powers of {{w11_power}} and {{w14_pow_w3}}. The mixture over-predicts the <i>size</i> of the move
in both directions ({{w14_resid_w11}} and {{w14_resid_w14}}).</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip ok">CAUSAL AT THE TEXT LEVEL [measured]</span>
<span class="claim">The belief-mixture is not a description of four cells; it is a dose-response
law — {{w14_dose_w11}} clarified, {{w14_dose_w3}} natural, {{w14_dose_w14}} degraded.
<span class="why">The degraded point's <i>comprehension</i> coordinate is [suggested], not
[measured]: the judge that produced it fails on exactly the wording that breaks the model, and
human calibration of it was pending at submission.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="node neu">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">A judge that fails exactly where the model fails</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>The design choice that caused it:</b> the direction judge is handed the prompt
and must work the bet's mapping out itself, so that one prompt serves both mirrored arms. Under
nested-negation wording it has to solve the same puzzle the model does.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> <b>{{lf_d051_wrong_k}} of {{lf_d051_wrong_n}}</b>
traces it labelled <code>correct</code> on one arm had landed on that arm's unfavoured side. An
independent regex instrument that never reads the mapping sentence agrees with it
{{lf_d051_w3_below}}/{{lf_d051_w3_above}} on natural wording and
<b>{{lf_d051_w14_below}}/{{lf_d051_w14_above}}</b> on degraded. On the frozen basis the
belief-conditional cells appear to collapse and cross ({{w14_corr_gap}}); on the calibrated basis
they do not move ({{lf_d051_regex_w14}} against {{lf_d051_regex_w3}} on the same quantity in the
original dataset).</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip no">READ ALONE, THE FROZEN TABLE SAYS THE OPPOSITE OF THE TRUTH</span>
<span class="claim">A judge and a subject that share a weakness cannot be used to measure that
weakness.
<span class="why">The first warning was on the invoice: those traces made the judge emit an order
of magnitude more output tokens than any prior packet's constant predicted, days before the
analysis noticed anything.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">Belief formation has no readable onset, and the curve that looked like one was length</span></div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> Sweeping a probe over every generated position of
{{w12_n_labelled}} labelled traces, the frozen onset criterion — {{w12_onset_k}} consecutive bins
above the null's {{w12_onset_pct}} percentile — <b>fires at no layer in any family</b>, and there
are <b>{{w12_flips}}</b> belief flips against a label-shuffled false-flip rate of
{{w12_falseflip}}. The one alignment that did rise is confounded: a probe with <i>one feature, the
trace's output length, and no activations at all</i>, reads {{lf_w12_lenonly}} on the same traces,
because traces that get the mapping wrong run {{lf_w12_len_delta}} tokens longer.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip op">MEASURED NULL, PLUS ONE RETRACTION</span>
<span class="claim">No readable onset and no flips at this resolving power — and any statistic
binned on trace fraction in this dataset is confounded with the outcome it predicts.
<span class="why">A targeted attack on the decodability result using that same confound was then
run and the result survived it, narrower than its own headline number.</span></span></div>
</div>

<div class="node">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">The belief transplant, and a design that could not have found anything</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>What was varied:</b> take two traces of the <i>same prompt</i> that formed
<i>opposite</i> beliefs and swap the belief component of one into the other — an operation that,
unlike injection, adds no norm-scale perturbation of its own. {{w15_n_pairs}} disjoint pairs per
direction, four arms, from {{n_w15_harvest}} fresh rollouts.</div>
<div class="res"><span class="rl">RESULT</span> <b>Δ_swap = {{w15_dswap}} [{{w15_dswap_lo}},
{{w15_dswap_hi}}]</b>, with the controls moving as much or more (Δ_self {{w15_dself}}, Δ_rand
{{w15_drand}}). <b>The qualification is larger than the result:</b> the pre-registered cut left
only {{w15_fin_frozen}} of {{w15_n_pairs}} landings still movable, because the locked-fraction
parameter that declared the design powered was measured on the original traces
({{lf_d055_lam_decl}}) rather than the regenerated continuations ({{lf_d055_lam_meas}}) — achieved
power {{lf_w15_pow_lo}}–{{lf_w15_pow_hi}} against the {{lf_w15_pow_decl_lo}}–{{lf_w15_pow_decl_hi}}
declared. A post-hoc diagnostic at full surface, where {{w15_val_deep}} of {{w15_n_pairs}} pairs
genuinely change their final number, reads Δ_swap {{w15_deep_swap}} [{{w15_deep_swap_lo}},
{{w15_deep_swap_hi}}] at power {{lf_jc4_pow_lo}}–{{lf_jc4_pow_hi}}.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip op">MEASURED NULL, BOUNDED BY A POST-HOC DIAGNOSTIC [suggested]</span>
<span class="claim">The belief state is not transplantable by this operation, and the null survives
its own bound.
<span class="why">The operation's own anatomy says why it may never have had a chance: at the
frozen layer the two belief classes are separated along this direction by
{{lf_d056_sep_sd}} of their own within-class spread, and the two arms whose difference
<i>is</i> the experiment differ from each other by about {{lf_w15_swapself}} —
{{lf_w15_ratio}}× smaller than the noise they sit in.</span></span></div>
</div>

<h2 class="uhead">Synthesis</h2>

<div class="node neu">
<div class="nh"><span class="nt">What the project establishes, in three sentences</span></div>
<div class="row"><b>Representational [measured].</b> The side a trace believes the bet favours is
linearly decodable from the residual stream at the model's own estimate positions, at
{{w5_B_balacc_lstar}} against a null {{lf_ci_pct}}th percentile of {{w5_B_null_lstar}}, and
{{w5_pre_verbal_pct}} % of the carrying points precede the moment the trace names a cause.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Causal [measured null].</b> Writing that direction back in, at six doses from
{{d_a025_pct}} % to {{d_a4_pct}} % of the residual-stream norm and against
{{n_null_directions}} matched random directions, produced no landing effect distinguishable from
what a random direction of the same size produces.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Causal at the text level [measured].</b> Rewriting the bet note to move
comprehension up and then down moved the landing gap both times, inside a prediction frozen on the
original cells both times, at distinguishing powers of {{w11_power}} and {{w14_pow_w3}}. Two
further activation-level operations — a low-dose ladder with matched nulls and a belief transplant
at {{w15_n_pairs}} pairs per direction — were null like the first.</div>
<div class="row"><b>Unresolved at the activation level [not tested at resolving power].</b> Two
possibilities remain open and no design here separates them: there is no direction-specific causal
effect, or there is one below the resolving power of every operation tried. One candidate
explanation is measured and is [suggested]: the direction all three interventions used separates
the two belief classes by {{lf_d056_sep_sd}} of their own within-class spread, so every one of
them ran through a channel with a low ceiling.</div>
<div class="verdict"><span class="chip op">ANSWERED IN ONE CHANNEL, OPEN IN THE OTHER</span>
<span class="claim">The model's belief about the favoured side drives its estimate through the text
channel, demonstrably; no one-dimensional activation-space handle on that belief was found, at any
operation or power this project could reach.
<span class="why">That is a real answer to the leaf the predecessor study left, and a sharper one
than the activation work alone could give: the belief is not decoration — it is load-bearing and
it was moved on purpose, twice, in opposite directions. What remains unshown is that the
<i>direction</i> found in the residual stream is the thing carrying it.</span></span></div>
</div>

<h2 class="uhead">Open leaves</h2>
<p class="lede">Each is a question a specific branch above raised and could not answer, with the
next step named.</p>

<div class="leaf"><b>Is the decoded direction causal at doses this design could not reach?</b>
The smallest pre-registered dose, {{d_a1_pct}} % of the residual-stream norm, already behaves
symmetrically in α, which is what a pure magnitude effect looks like; the follow-up went down to
{{d_a025_pct}} % and found a flat, direction-independent offset with no gradient in dose. Closing
it needs a ladder below these doses at a sample far above {{conv_n_per_arm}} per arm, with every
frozen threshold simulated under its own null before it is frozen.
<span class="from">→ from the intervention and its follow-up</span></div>

<div class="leaf"><b>Would a distributed or nonlinear transplant reach what a single direction
could not?</b> Patching rather than injecting was the leaf the dose anatomy raised, and it was
run: swapping the belief component between same-prompt traces that believed opposite things is
null, at {{w15_n_pairs}} pairs per direction and with a post-hoc bound at full surface. What that
leaves is the <i>dimensionality</i>: the coordinate all three operations used separates the belief
classes by only {{lf_d056_sep_sd}} of their within-class spread, so the next experiment has to
estimate the belief subspace with a method that can hold more than one dimension and move the
whole subspace, not one projection.
<span class="from">→ from the dose anatomy, and from the transplant that closed its first form</span></div>

<div class="leaf"><b>How wrong is the judge on the wording it was actually run on?</b> The
direction judge and the model fail the same reasoning step, so agreement measured on one wording
({{lf_d051_w3_below}}–{{lf_d051_w3_above}}) did not transfer to another
({{lf_d051_w14_below}}/{{lf_d051_w14_above}}). A blinded {{lf_hl_rows}}-row human-label packet was
built, sealed and sent to close this and had not returned by submission — the cheapest open item
on this list.
<span class="from">→ from the degraded-wording arm; the degraded point is [suggested] until it returns</span></div>

<div class="leaf"><b>Why is one mirror of the same bet so much harder to understand?</b>
"Do not exceed the threshold and a good cause benefits" is understood
{{w3_correct_A_below}} % of the time; "exceed the threshold and a good cause benefits" only
{{w3_correct_A_above}} %. That asymmetry is large, cheap to measure, and it is what makes the
aggregate landing gap in this model class a mixture rather than an effect.
<span class="from">→ from the behavioural phenotype</span></div>

<div class="leaf"><b>Where does covertness come from?</b> A model of this size announces the bet in
{{w3_mention_pct}} % of traces while the {{lf_panel_size}}B panel almost never does. Scale, model
family, tuning and prompt surface are all confounded across the two studies, and nothing here can
separate them.
<span class="from">→ from the behavioural phenotype; tiered [suggested] throughout</span></div>

